<article class="env-exercise" id="0E9H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E9H">Exercise <span data-tag="0E9H">111.32.11</span>.</a> Give an example of a topological space $X$ and a functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X) \longrightarrow \textit{Sets}  \]
</div>
  <p> which is exact (commutes with finite products and equalizers and commutes with finite coproducts and coequalizers, see Categories, Section <a href="/tag/0033" data-tag="0033">4.23</a>), but there is no point $x \in X$ such that $F$ is isomorphic to the stalk functor $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \mathcal{F}_ x$. </p>
</article>